1
00:00:00,182 --> 00:00:03,312
(Howard:)It's smashed beyond repair.
What are you gonna do with it?

2
00:00:03,894 --> 00:00:07,184
(Raj:)What else?
Sell it on eBay as slightly used.

3
00:00:07,689 --> 00:00:09,979
(Leonard:)It was Penny's boyfriend's.
They broke up.

4
00:00:10,150 --> 00:00:14,030
(Howard:)Apparently, he posted intimate details
of their physical relationship on his blog...

5
00:00:14,196 --> 00:00:17,236
(Howard:)...which I cannot find anywhere.

6
00:00:18,033 --> 00:00:20,913
You know what? I'm gonna go back
and try talking to her again.

7
00:00:21,077 --> 00:00:24,117
(Howard:)Good idea.
Sit with her, hold her, comfort her.

8
00:00:24,289 --> 00:00:28,499
(Howard:)And if the moment feels right,
see if you can cop a feel.

9
00:00:30,337 --> 00:00:31,917
(Leonard:)I'm not going to do that, Howard.

10
00:00:32,088 --> 00:00:35,888
(Sheldon:)I'm not aware of any social convention
that requires you to intervene at all.

11
00:00:36,051 --> 00:00:37,841
What about damsel in distress?

12
00:00:38,011 --> 00:00:41,641
Twelfth-century code of chivalry?
Not exactly current.

13
00:00:42,057 --> 00:00:44,767
(Sheldon:)You'd also have to be knighted
for that to apply.

14
00:00:45,602 --> 00:00:47,852
(Leonard:)I don't care.
She's upset, I'm going over there.

15
00:00:48,021 --> 00:00:51,401
(Howard:)Remember to sit on your hands a bit
so they're warm.

16
00:00:52,484 --> 00:00:55,824
(Leonard:)I'm her friend. I'm not going
to take advantage of her vulnerability.

17
00:00:56,821 --> 00:01:00,241
So you're saying, if in the depths of despair
she throws herself at you...

